  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_003 (multimodal, scgpt+imagenet_vit_l, concat) achieves 0.4348 acc, only marginally above RNA-only config_004 (0.4106), while image-only config_025 is very weak (0.2266). This small multimodal gain raises the question of whether the image signal is genuinely useful but poorly integrated, or simply uninformative. Question: config_031 changes only the fusion strategy (concat → weighted) while holding all other settings identical to config_003 (multimodal, singleprofile, scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, no aggregation). This isolates the effect of fusion on multimodal performance. Why this is the best next experiment: It is a single-variable comparison that directly tests whether a learned weighting can extract more value from the image modality. If weighted fusion improves over concat, it confirms the image carries useful signal and justifies further investment in multimodal configurations (aggregation, multiprofile, alternative encoders). If it does not, it strongly suggests the image modality with imagenet_vit_l is not contributing meaningfully, redirecting the remaining budget toward RNA encoder or profile-setting improvements. Under a limited budget, resolving this uncertainty about whether multimodal fusion is worth pursuing is the highest-value information gain."
}

